  "notes": "{気|き}になる is an idiomatic expression meaning to be on one's mind or to bother someone.\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. To worry about: {結果|けっか}が{気|き}になる (worried about results)\n2. To be interested in: あの{人|ひと}が{気|き}になる (interested in that person)\n3. To be bothered by: {音|おと}が{気|き}になる (bothered by a sound)\n\nCONTRAST WITH {気|き}にする:\n- {気|き}になる: something weighs on your mind (unintentional)\n- {気|き}にする: to actively worry about or care about (intentional)\n\nNote: The subject is the thing that concerns you, marked with が.",
